b/ref 1069 "q-144847" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570710 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570710 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/86/861e191e0f0b0d993e2d16f29da17ec9e258d657f6bdfc471e5fa9cf21a67b21.png)\n\nThe function $f(x)$ is defined and differentiable on $[-3,2].$ The graph of ${f}^{′}(x),$ the derivative of $f(x),$ is shown above. Find the maximum value of the function $f(x)$ on the interval $[-3,2]$ given that $f(2)=4.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570710 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "25bfd26a-4014-54ec-bb25-41bebf6a0072" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570710 #edb/ref 1074 "According to the candidates test, the maximum value of $f(x)$ on $[-3,2]$ must occur at a critical point or an endpoint of the interval. \n\n**Step 1**: Find the critical points:\n\nWe see that ${f}^{′}(x)$ is defined everywhere on $x\\in (-3,2),$ and ${f}^{′}(x)=0$ at $x=-1$ Therefore, the candidates are $x=-3,-1,2.$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the value of $f$ for each candidate using the fundamental theorem of calculus:\n\nThe function is made up of $1$ trapezoid and $1$ triangle. Let's add the areas bounded by these shapes to our diagram:\n\n![](images/b7/b7f6e2f43ae474ec3194b2395144e8ea7dc9964da65bd018af08bb24b873bdd4.png)\n\nUsing the given information and the fundamental theorem of calculus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(2) & =4 \\\\ f(-1) & =f(2)+{\\int }_{2}^{-1}{f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =f(2)-{\\int }_{-1}^{2}{f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4-5 \\\\  & =-1 \\\\ f(-3) & =f(2)+{\\int }_{2}^{-3}{f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =f(2)-{\\int }_{-3}^{2}{f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4-(-1+5) \\\\  & =4-4 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Select the largest value of $f$ from our candidates. \n\nComparing the values of $f$ found in step $2,$ we have\n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{max}}=max\\{4,-1,0\\}=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the maximum value of $f$ is ${f}_{\\text{max}}=4,$ and the value of $x$ that maximizes $f(x)$ is ${x}_{\\text{max}}=2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570734 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186570600 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570734 #edb/ref 1069 "q-144875" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570734 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570734 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/cb/cba90791c239c986390a8a7fe1cb3ea0b4abb9cfd86ca13cba9ece6a5b4860b6.png)\n\nThe function $f(x)$ is defined and differentiable on $[-5,4].$ The graph of ${f}^{′}(x),$ the derivative of $f(x),$ is shown above. Find the minimum value of the function $f(x)$ on the interval $[-5,4]$ given that $f(4)=1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570734 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5fcb87aa-38a0-5213-a001-cd7978756f39" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570734 #edb/ref 1074 "According to the candidates test, the minimum value of $f(x)$ on $[-5,4]$ must occur at a critical point or an endpoint of the interval. \n\n**Step 1**: Find the critical points:\n\nWe see that ${f}^{′}(x)$ is defined everywhere on $x\\in (-5,4),$ and ${f}^{′}(x)=0$ at $x=0.$ Therefore, the candidates are $x=-5,0,4.$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the value of $f$ for each candidate using the fundamental theorem of calculus:\n\nThe function is made up of $1$ trapezoid and $2$ triangles. Let's add the areas bounded by these shapes to our diagram:\n\n![](images/a8/a8bff8783c0e536cd0e3c475a8fca87a9861a1e1f0ca7f2833ca9c434da2426d.png)\n\nUsing the given information and the fundamental theorem of calculus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(4) & =1 \\\\ f(0) & =f(4)+{\\int }_{4}^{0}{f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =f(4)-{\\int }_{0}^{4}{f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =1-(-8) \\\\  & =1+8 \\\\  & =9 \\\\ f(-5) & =f(4)+{\\int }_{4}^{-5}{f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =f(4)-{\\int }_{-5}^{4}{f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =1-(9+2-8) \\\\  & =1-3 \\\\  & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Select the smallest value of $f$ from our candidates. \n\nComparing the values of $f$ found in step $2,$ we have\n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{min}}=min\\{1,9,-2\\}=-2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the minimum value of $f$ is ${f}_{\\text{min}}=-2,$ and the value of $x$ that minimizes $f(x)$ is ${x}_{\\text{min}}=-5.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570778 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186570649 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570778 #edb/ref 1069 "q-344165" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570778 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570778 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/73/731237ee8d4ea5fdb53c50971bad11dd9f4317f595ae9af95846b17b6d064fce.png)\n\nThe function $g(x)$ is defined and differentiable on $[-5,3].$ The graph of ${g}^{′}(x),$ the derivative of $g(x),$ is shown above, where the area of the region between the graph and the $x$-axis is $7.$\n\nGiven that $g(3)=4,$ what is the minimum value ${g}_{\\text{min}}$ of $g(x)$ on the interval $[-5,3]?$\n\n${g}_{\\text{min}}=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570778 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "df0b416e-f70a-5924-a6c6-f62bc6887f2f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570778 #edb/ref 1074 "According to the candidates test, the minimum value of $g(x)$ on $[-5,3]$ must occur at a critical point or an endpoint of the interval.\n\n**Step 1**: Find the critical points:\n\nWe see that ${g}^{′}(x)$ is defined everywhere on $x\\in (-5,3),$ and ${g}^{′}(x)\\ne 0$ inside the interval. Therefore, the candidates are $x=-5,3.$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the value of $g$ for each candidate using the fundamental theorem of calculus:\n\nUsing the given information and the fundamental theorem of calculus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(3) & =4 \\\\ g(-5) & =g(3)+{\\int }_{3}^{-5}{g}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =g(3)-{\\int }_{-5}^{3}{g}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4-7 \\\\  & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Select the smallest value of $g$ from our candidates.\n\nComparing the values of $g$ found in step $2,$ we have\n\n$$\n{g}_{\\text{min}}=min\\{4,-3\\}=-3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the minimum value of $g$ is ${g}_{\\text{min}}=-3,$ and the value of $x$ that minimizes $g(x)$ is ${x}_{\\text{min}}=-5.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570796 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186570865 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570796 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "0a11be39-e15b-5695-a209-6aa5aa9d56b2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570796 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186570710 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570831 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "6c8a0b71-476e-5aff-ab08-21790a69690d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570831 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186570778 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570865 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186570831 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570865 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "dcee01d3-9728-5373-bd94-47606309bf0a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570865 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186570734 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
